# Your publications, one DOI per line. Bare DOIs — no https://doi.org/ prefix.
# Comments and blank lines are ignored. Delete these examples and use your own.
#
# Easiest way to build this: put your CV or publication list in ../input/ and ask an
# LLM to extract every DOI, one per line. Then check the count against your CV.
#
# Watch for tracking parameters. A DOI copied from a publisher page often arrives as
# 10.1234/abcd?utm_source=... or ?sharing_token=... — those 404 and the paper silently
# disappears from the harvest. Strip everything from the "?" onwards.
#
# Anything below the #PREPRINTS marker is ignored by harvest, so park preprints of
# already-published work there rather than deleting them.

10.1126/science.275.5301.810
10.1103/physrevlett.93.268104

#PREPRINTS
10.1101/2025.01.01.000000
